Restarted database container in background task. Waiting for completion to inspect listener state.
The target service `database` is not listening on port 5432 (declared contract: `tcp://database:5432`). Inspection of the container script shows that it checks for `/state/broken` (mounted read-only from persistent state). A bounded restart attempt confirmed that `httpd -p 5432` remains closed and does not recover. Because this failure is persistent across restart/recreate and cannot be resolved by standard container infrastructure repair without file/state mutation, we abstain.

{"status":"ABSTAINED","diagnosis":"TARGET_NOT_LISTENING","notes":"Target service listener on port 5432 remains closed after container restart due to persistent state."}
